---
import Card from "astro-theme-university/components/Card.astro";
import CardGrid from "astro-theme-university/components/CardGrid.astro";
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import heroImage from "../assets/images/hero-home.avif";
import { courseMeta } from "../course-config";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../site-config";
---

<ContentLayout
  title={`${courseMeta.code}: ${courseMeta.title}`}
  description={courseMeta.description}
  heroImage={heroImage}
  heroImageAlt="A row of shipping boxes on a receding line, flat gold and black shapes on warm cream, in a two-ink risograph print"
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <ul class="course-tags" aria-label="Course tags">
    {courseMeta.tags.map((tag) => <li>{tag}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2>What you will do</h2>
  <p>
    Pull apart real packages — an oversized retail box, a compliance-labelled
    parcel, a brand unboxing — and work out which of three design logics
    actually produced them: brand experience, logistics cost, or compliance.
    From week 4 you trade guesswork for numbers: Australia Post's cubic-weight
    formula, ISTA 3A drop-test standards, and a real return-rate calculation,
    applied to the packages you tore down in week 1. You walk out with a
    packaging cost model you built and tested against a real product, and an
    answer — argued from evidence, not vibes — to the course's throughline
    claim that sustainability language on packaging is mostly marketing.
  </p>

  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <p>
    Anyone who sells things online, or wants to: the course assumes no prior
    knowledge of packaging engineering, freight pricing, or logistics, but
    does assume you're comfortable with basic arithmetic and reading a spec
    sheet. If you've ever wondered why your order arrived in a box big enough
    for a microwave, this course explains it — and asks you to decide whether
    the explanation should change how you'd package something yourself.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to go next</h2>
  <CardGrid columns={2}>
    <Card title={sessionLabels.plural} href="/sessions/">
      <p>The weekly schedule and what happens in each teaching session.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Assessment" href="/assessments/">
      <p>What is marked, what it is worth, and when it is due.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="People" href="/people/">
      <p>Who teaches the course and how to reach them.</p>
    </Card>
  </CardGrid>
</ContentLayout>

<style>
  .course-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-block: 0 2rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .course-tags li {
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    background: var(--at-bg-alt);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
